The runtime scoring service uses only Python 3.12 standard-library modules.
Its Docker image uses the official `python:3.12.10-slim` image and installs no
third-party Python packages. Offline model training uses `scikit-learn==1.9.1`
from `requirements-ml.txt`; it is not installed in the runtime image.

The included `scoring/artifacts/logreg_v1.json` is a project-trained logistic
regression model, not a third-party pretrained model. Its training and test data
in `data/synthetic_v1/` were generated by this project using the reproducible
generator described in `docs/SYNTHETIC_ML.md`. `rules_v1` is a project-defined
alternative. No real customer dataset or paid API is used.

Company and credit-bureau inputs are synthetic. FNS and BKI integrations are
simulated by the surrounding backend application, not by this service. The
consolidated component and service inventory is in the root `smart-credit`
repository's `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES`.
